====Usage notes====
*Unlike the English distinction between ''make'' and ''do'', the verb {{m|de|machen|t=[[make]]}} can be used as a synonym for {{m|de|tun|t=[[do]]}} in most cases. However, ''tun'' cannot be used for the proper senses of ''machen''.
*The verb ''machen'' can be combined with many different nouns to create various expressions. These can often be translated into English with [[make]] or [[take]]. For many of these expressions, a more specific verb is available and is usually preferred in formal or written language.
*: {{coi|de|Angaben machen|to provide information}}
*: {{coi|de|eine Aufzeichnung machen|to keep a record}}
*: {{coi|de|Ausflüchte machen|to make excuses}}
*: {{coi|de|Bankrott/Pleite machen|to go bankrupt}}
*: {{coi|de|eine Besorgung machen|to run an errand}}
*: {{coi|de|ein Bett machen|to make a bed}}
*: {{coi|de|Feierabend machen|to call it a day}}
*: {{coi|de|Ferien machen|to take a vacation, to go on holiday}}
*: {{coi|de|ein Feuer machen|to light a fire}}
*: {{coi|de|ein Foto machen|to take a picture}}
*: {{coi|de|Fortschritte machen|to make headway}}
*: {{coi|de|Gewinn machen|to turn a profit}}
*: {{coi|de|Kasse machen|to cash in}}
*: {{coi|de|einen Krach machen|to make a racket}}
*: {{coi|de|einen Kurs machen|to take a course}}
*: {{coi|de|Notizen machen|to take notes}}
*: {{coi|de|Platz machen|to make room}}
*: {{coi|de|eine Reise machen|to take a trip}}
*: {{coi|de|Schluss machen|to call it quits}}
*: {{coi|de|Spaß machen|to be fun}}
*: {{coi|de|Überstunden machen|to do overtime}}
*: {{coi|de|Witze machen|to joke}}

